<p begin="04:19:04.479" end="04:19:07.920" style="s2">declared that she had opposed this team</p>
<p begin="04:19:06.239" end="04:19:10.080" style="s2">lineup from the beginning. As the</p>
<p begin="04:19:07.920" end="04:19:12.080" style="s2">argument continued, Zeke quietly asked</p>
<p begin="04:19:10.080" end="04:19:14.080" style="s2">Laya if she was truly okay with all of</p>
<p begin="04:19:12.080" end="04:19:16.000" style="s2">this. Laya responded that it didn&#39;t</p>
<p begin="04:19:14.080" end="04:19:18.000" style="s2">bother her. She was simply glad to be</p>
<p begin="04:19:16.000" end="04:19:20.159" style="s2">part of the mission. Zeke laughed,</p>
<p begin="04:19:18.000" end="04:19:21.600" style="s2">commenting on her big heart. While Sandy</p>
<p begin="04:19:20.159" end="04:19:23.359" style="s2">continued to press the issue,</p>
<p begin="04:19:21.600" end="04:19:25.920" style="s2">questioning Leica&#39;s decision to include</p>
<p begin="04:19:23.359" end="04:19:27.840" style="s2">Vanil and Allen. Leica hesitated, but</p>
<p begin="04:19:25.920" end="04:19:29.520" style="s2">admitted that while she had her doubts,</p>
<p begin="04:19:27.840" end="04:19:31.680" style="s2">their strength made them necessary for</p>
<p begin="04:19:29.520" end="04:19:33.439" style="s2">the mission. Alan agreed, praising</p>
