<p begin="04:22:31.359" end="04:22:35.920" style="s2">Veneil, asking why he couldn&#39;t have made</p>
<p begin="04:22:33.439" end="04:22:37.840" style="s2">their landing gentler, but Venil coldly</p>
<p begin="04:22:35.920" end="04:22:40.319" style="s2">replied that it wasn&#39;t his problem.</p>
<p begin="04:22:37.840" end="04:22:42.239" style="s2">After climbing down from the tree, Edges</p>
<p begin="04:22:40.319" end="04:22:43.760" style="s2">pointed out that Vanil and Allan had</p>
<p begin="04:22:42.239" end="04:22:46.319" style="s2">already softened the impact for</p>
<p begin="04:22:43.760" end="04:22:49.040" style="s2">everyone, and considering the situation,</p>
<p begin="04:22:46.319" end="04:22:51.359" style="s2">things could have gone much worse. Laya,</p>
<p begin="04:22:49.040" end="04:22:54.000" style="s2">wincing in pain, muttered that it still</p>
<p begin="04:22:51.359" end="04:22:56.319" style="s2">hurt. But at least she was alive. Taking</p>
<p begin="04:22:54.000" end="04:22:58.159" style="s2">a moment to process everything, Edges</p>
<p begin="04:22:56.319" end="04:23:00.319" style="s2">reflected on what had just happened.</p>
<p begin="04:22:58.159" end="04:23:02.720" style="s2">Being thrown into the rift, falling from</p>
<p begin="04:23:00.319" end="04:23:05.040" style="s2">the sky, and then watching a giant bird</p>
<p begin="04:23:02.720" end="04:23:06.880" style="s2">snatch Zeke away. With a sigh, he</p>
<p begin="04:23:05.040" end="04:23:09.120" style="s2">commented that entering a rift like this</p>
<p begin="04:23:06.880" end="04:23:11.199" style="s2">was far rougher than he expected.</p>
<p begin="04:23:09.120" end="04:23:13.199" style="s2">Realizing they had no idea what might</p>
<p begin="04:23:11.199" end="04:23:15.040" style="s2">happen next, he suggested they drink</p>
<p begin="04:23:13.199" end="04:23:17.439" style="s2">their healing potions while they had the</p>
<p begin="04:23:15.040" end="04:23:19.600" style="s2">chance. Sandy and Laya immediately</p>
<p begin="04:23:17.439" end="04:23:21.680" style="s2">followed his advice while Leica turned</p>
<p begin="04:23:19.600" end="04:23:23.279" style="s2">to Venil and Allan to thank them,</p>
<p begin="04:23:21.680" end="04:23:25.760" style="s2">acknowledging that they had saved</p>
<p begin="04:23:23.279" end="04:23:27.760" style="s2">everyone back there. Both Alan and Venil</p>
<p begin="04:23:25.760" end="04:23:30.159" style="s2">were briefly stunned, clearly not</p>
<p begin="04:23:27.760" end="04:23:32.159" style="s2">expecting her gratitude. Venil turned</p>
<p begin="04:23:30.159" end="04:23:34.159" style="s2">away and muttered that if they lost</p>
<p begin="04:23:32.159" end="04:23:36.319" style="s2">people here and failed the mission, it</p>
<p begin="04:23:34.159" end="04:23:38.080" style="s2">would only cause more trouble. Sandy</p>
<p begin="04:23:36.319" end="04:23:39.920" style="s2">crossed her arms and complained that he</p>
<p begin="04:23:38.080" end="04:23:42.720" style="s2">could at least accept a simple thank</p>
<p begin="04:23:39.920" end="04:23:44.640" style="s2">you. Alan, trying to refocus the group,</p>
<p begin="04:23:42.720" end="04:23:46.319" style="s2">asked what their next move should be,</p>
<p begin="04:23:44.640" end="04:23:48.399" style="s2">mentioning that Lord Zeke had been</p>
<p begin="04:23:46.319" end="04:23:50.880" style="s2">carried off somewhere. With a dark</p>
<p begin="04:23:48.399" end="04:23:53.199" style="s2">expression, Vanil bluntly suggested they</p>
<p begin="04:23:50.880" end="04:23:54.720" style="s2">could just leave Zeke behind. Laya</p>
<p begin="04:23:53.199" end="04:23:56.800" style="s2">immediately questioned if he was</p>
<p begin="04:23:54.720" end="04:23:59.520" style="s2">actually worried, but Venil brushed her</p>
<p begin="04:23:56.800" end="04:24:02.000" style="s2">off, trying to hide his true feelings.</p>
<p begin="04:23:59.520" end="04:24:04.560" style="s2">Sandy scoffed, saying he was terrible at</p>
<p begin="04:24:02.000" end="04:24:06.720" style="s2">being honest, but unexpectedly, Edges</p>
<p begin="04:24:04.560" end="04:24:08.720" style="s2">sided with Venil. He explained that</p>
<p begin="04:24:06.720" end="04:24:11.279" style="s2">worrying about Zeke right now was likely</p>
<p begin="04:24:08.720" end="04:24:12.960" style="s2">a waste of energy. Annoyed, Sandy</p>
<p begin="04:24:11.279" end="04:24:15.520" style="s2">demanded to know how he could agree with</p>
<p begin="04:24:12.960" end="04:24:17.760" style="s2">Veneil, but Leica also backed him up,</p>
<p begin="04:24:15.520" end="04:24:19.920" style="s2">calmly, stating that if it was Zeke, he</p>
<p begin="04:24:17.760" end="04:24:22.159" style="s2">would be fine on his own. In fact, they</p>
<p begin="04:24:19.920" end="04:24:24.159" style="s2">were probably the ones in more danger.</p>
<p begin="04:24:22.159" end="04:24:26.239" style="s2">Sandy fell silent for a moment before</p>
<p begin="04:24:24.159" end="04:24:28.800" style="s2">asking what they even thought of Zeke.</p>
<p begin="04:24:26.239" end="04:24:31.199" style="s2">One by one, they all paused, recalling</p>
