<p begin="05:59:42.798" end="05:59:46.558" style="s2">yet. Still laughing to himself, Luden</p>
<p begin="05:59:45.200" end="05:59:48.240" style="s2">remarked that now that Mench had</p>
<p begin="05:59:46.558" end="05:59:50.480" style="s2">arrived, he would leave first and</p>
<p begin="05:59:48.240" end="05:59:52.240" style="s2">finally get some muchneeded sleep. Freya</p>
<p begin="05:59:50.480" end="05:59:53.760" style="s2">immediately asked him to stay until</p>
<p begin="05:59:52.240" end="05:59:55.680" style="s2">everything had been settled. But the</p>
<p begin="05:59:53.760" end="05:59:57.760" style="s2">moment she turned around, Luden had</p>
<p begin="05:59:55.680" end="05:59:59.920" style="s2">already disappeared without a trace.</p>
<p begin="05:59:57.760" end="06:00:01.600" style="s2">Seeing this, Menrich simply commented</p>
<p begin="05:59:59.920" end="06:00:03.760" style="s2">that Luden had always been a free</p>
<p begin="06:00:01.600" end="06:00:05.360" style="s2">spirit. Menrich then turned toward Zeke</p>
<p begin="06:00:03.760" end="06:00:07.520" style="s2">and assured him that from this point</p>
<p begin="06:00:05.360" end="06:00:09.200" style="s2">onward, they would remain by his side,</p>
